.Dd November 9, 2026
.Dt VTESTRELAY 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm vtestrelay
.Nd carry Mesa's vtest protocol from its local socket to a server over TCP
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl 1v
.Op Fl s Ar socket
.Ar host port
.Nm
.Fl -version
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
listens on a Unix socket for Mesa's vtest client, the
.Cm virpipe
driver, and carries each client's connection to the vtest server at
.Ar host
and
.Ar port
over TCP.
It forks a child for each client, which connects to the server, relays both
directions until both have ended and exits.
.Pp
The client always asks for the newest protocol, and the newer protocols
pass file descriptors on the socket, which a network connection cannot carry.
.Nm
therefore drops the client's version query,
.Dv VCMD_PING_PROTOCOL_VERSION .
The server sees only the busy wait that the client sends behind it and
answers that first, which the client takes for a server of protocol 0.
Under protocol 0 every resource's contents, transfers in and out alike,
travel in the stream, and a fence is a busy wait on the server.
.Pp
.Nm
reads the client's commands to find the query, and refuses a command that
protocol 0 has not, or one before
.Dv VCMD_CREATE_RENDERER ,
by closing both connections.
It passes the server's replies on unread.
The words of a command are in the machine's own byte order, so both ends must
share it.
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl 1
Relay the first client in the listening process and exit with its status,
removing the socket.
.It Fl s Ar socket
Listen on
.Ar socket
instead of the path that
.Ev VTEST_SOCKET_NAME
names, or
.Pa /tmp/.virgl_test
when it is unset, which is where Mesa's client connects by default.
A socket file left at that path by a relay that has ended is removed; a path
where a server answers, or one that is not a socket, is refused.
.It Fl v
Report the socket on start, and each connection's command counts by kind and
its bytes in each direction when it ends, as a
.Ql "vtestrelay: result:"
line on standard error.
.It Fl -version
Print the relay's version and the protocol it keeps to, and exit.
.El
.Pp
.Dv SIGTERM ,
.Dv SIGINT
and
.Dv SIGHUP
stop the listening process, which removes the socket; a child goes on until
its client ends.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev VTEST_SOCKET_NAME
The socket to listen on, as Mesa's client reads it.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 when the relay was stopped by a signal, or with
.Fl 1
when the client's connection ended cleanly; 1 on an error or a refused
command; 2 on a usage error.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Draw with Mesa's
.Cm virpipe
on a vtest server whose TCP port 5555 QEMU forwards to the host's port
10555:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
vtestrelay -s /tmp/vtest.sock 127.0.0.1 10555 &
VTEST_SOCKET_NAME=/tmp/vtest.sock LIBGL_ALWAYS_SOFTWARE=1 \e
    GALLIUM_DRIVER=virpipe eglinfo -p surfaceless
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
The source,
.Pa bed/vtestrelay.c ,
and
.Pa bed/Readme.md
in Rach2's tree, which describes the guest that serves vtest.
